WEBVTT

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:06.470
Yusei Fudo already summoned his 
ace monster Stardust Dragon!

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.650
It's okay.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.460
Even though he summoned Stardust, 
it's in defense position.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.730
Yeah.  There's no need to get flustered.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.800
Zushin the Sleeping Giant's 
attack points are equal

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.700
to the opponent's monster 
in battle plus 1000 points.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.900
Even Yusei can't attack carelessly.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.100
No matter what you try, it's pointless!

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.880
Nothing in the world can defeat Zushin!

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.110
Zushin!

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.900
How can he overcome this huge disadvantage?

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:41.320
Zushin the Sleeping Giant is invincible.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.250
It can't be targeted by spells or traps.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.060
It also negates the effects 
of the monster it battles.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.660
But Yusei must have a plan.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:52.690
Yeah.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.400
We're counting on you, Yusei!

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.970
Yusei, here I go!

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.170
My turn!

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:05.540
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:14.450
By removing 4 Speed Counters, you take 800 
points of damage for every Speed Spell in my hand!

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:24.670
Zushin the Sleeping Giant 
attacks Stardust Dragon!

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.830
Stardust Dragon has 2500 attack points.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.430
By adding 1000 points, Zushin 
has 3500 attack points!

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.510
Feel the Sleeping Giant's power!

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.650
Zushin Punch!

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.950
I activate the trap Power Shift!

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.120
A trap?  Too bad, but trap 
cards can't target Zushin!

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.730
This trap isn't targeting Zushin!

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:56.590
What?

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:02.320
Power Shift makes one of my monsters' attack 
points become 0 until the End Phase!

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.050
He lowered Stardust Dragon's attack points?

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:10.910
That means Zushin's attack points are…

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.580
1000?

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.290
Stardust Dragon has 2000 defense points!

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.050
All right, Yusei!

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:30.970
Nicely done!  If Stardust's attack points 
decrease, Zushin's attack points also decrease!

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:37.800
So if he has more defense points, Zushin's 
attack is deflected, and the opponent takes damage.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.440
Impressive, Yusei!

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:44.270
The real battle is just starting!

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.250
Riding Duels.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.390
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:58.260
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:19.540
Reach out your hand and 
grab a bright tomorrow

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:29.650
Soar in the infinite skies  BELIEVE IN NEXUS

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:35.890
No one can stop my wild impulses

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:41.870
My hand sweats as the battle 
intensifies  This Heart Beat

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.640
I can't avoid this fearsome battle

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:53.240
I don't want it to end here  Go For It!!

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:59.620
Stand up  Don't tremble in fear alone

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:05.420
Remember that you have 
friends waiting for you

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:11.730
I'm not scared and I'll never give 
up, no matter how powerful the enemy

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:18.040
With real courage, I'll never lose

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:47.430
Trusted Power!
Zushin the Sleeping Giant vs Shooting Star Dragon

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:55.660
I can't believe he used 
Zushin's effect against me.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.830
But I have my own tricks!

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:01.280
I activate the trap Attack and Receive!

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:08.070
When I take damage, you 
take 700 points of damage!

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.500
I set one card and end my turn!

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:19.660
Power Shift's effect ends, so Stardust 
Dragon's attack points return to normal.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.800
Zushin can't be stopped that easily.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.980
Do you have another plan?

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.530
Taro is right.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.970
There aren't many strategies 
to defeat Zushin.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.480
But I must find one to defeat it!

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.560
My turn!

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.350
This card…

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.570
I summon Turbo Synchron in defense position!

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.080
Then I set two cards and end my turn.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:03.110
The only thing he did this turn was 
summon a monster in defense position!

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:08.680
Is even Yusei Fudo powerless 
against Zushin the Sleeping Giant?

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.610
That's right!  Zushin's 
power has no weaknesses!

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.790
Everyone is cheering for Team Taiyo.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.390
Damn!

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.890
Yusei, don't lose!

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:22.090
Team 5D's, don't lose!

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.850
Taiyo!

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.100
Everyone is cheering for us!

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:30.420
Can you hear them, Taro?

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:39.380
Do your best, Team Taiyo!

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:43.510
Everyone is cheering for Team Taiyo.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.650
The three of us entered the 
tournament with just one

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:52.890
D-Wheel and a bunch of Normal 
Cards that everyone has.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:01.330
We're not famous, and no one cared about us.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:08.880
But we're now on this grand stage 
and giving it our all in this duel!

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:19.530
As long as I believe in my friends 
and myself, we will definitely win.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.010
Even the impossible will become possible.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:29.550
With just a single desire, anyone in 
the world can shine into the future!

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.330
We're proof of that!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:37.340
I want to keep testing my strength!

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.720
I want to know how far I can go!

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:44.370
Yusei, that's why we must win this duel!

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.330
My turn!

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.310
I flip over my trap card Meteorain!

00:07:55.780 --> 00:08:02.170
If my monster attacks a monster in defense 
position, it can deal piercing damage this turn!

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.340
Zushin the Sleeping Giant 
has 3500 attack points!

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.850
Yusei, this is our entire power!

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:16.330
Zushin the Sleeping Giant 
attacks Stardust Dragon!

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:19.670
Go!  Zushin Punch!

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:20.430
This is bad!

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:24.770
If he takes this attack, he'll 
only have 1000 life points left!

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:26.270
Yusei!

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:30.050
I activate the Continuous 
Trap Graceful Revival!

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:32.790
What?

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:38.090
Graceful Revival Special Summons a Level 
2-or-below monster from my graveyard!

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:41.030
Resurrect, Tuningware!

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:49.410
I activate the trap card Urgent Tuning!

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:54.060
This card allows me to Synchro Summon 
a Synchro Monster during battle!

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.520
What?

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.950
Level 1 Turbo Synchron 
tunes Level 1 Tuningware!

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:05.320
The wishes come together to 
invite a new world of speed!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.220
Become the path that lights the way!

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:09.480
Synchro Summon!

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.790
The Synchro Tuner with the power 
of hope!  Formula Synchron!

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:17.740
Formula Synchron?

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:20.440
A Synchro Monster that's also a Tuner.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.250
Yusei, are you planning to…

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:28.110
Since Tuningware was sent to the 
graveyard due to a Synchro Summon...

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.480
I get to draw one card from my deck!

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:36.850
Taro, Team Taiyo is a powerful 
opponent.  You awakened

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:40.170
the Sleeping Giant for the 
first time in dueling history.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.270
In order to defeat you, 
I'll also use all my power!

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:07.410
Yusei, what are you planning to do?

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:16.100
The power to defeat the 
invincible Sleeping Giant...

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:19.970
To gain the power to make 
the impossible possible…

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:24.750
I have to overcome my limits.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:32.640
Clear Mind!

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:39.980
Level 2 Synchro Tuner Formula Synchron tunes 
Level 8 Synchro Monster Stardust Dragon!

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:48.030
Dreams crystallize to open 
a new door of evolution!

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:49.870
Become the path that lights the way!

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:54.060
Accel Synchro!

00:10:58.930 --> 00:10:59.930
He vanished?

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:01.600
Arise!

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.180
Shooting Star Dragon!

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:34.530
Accel Synchro!

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:35.640
That's…

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.740
Shooting Star Dragon!

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:41.400
Yusei, you're incredible.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:45.770
You managed to Synchro Summon during your 
opponent's turn without using a trap.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:48.790
But I won't show any mercy!

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:51.290
Zushin the Sleeping Giant is invincible!

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:53.690
Attack Shooting Star Dragon!

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:57.620
Shooting Star Dragon has 3300 attack points!

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:03.330
After adding 1000 points, Zushin the 
Sleeping Giant has 4300 attack points!

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.700
No matter how rare the card, it 
can't stand up against Zushin!

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.960
Go, Zushin!

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:13.510
I activate Shooting Star Dragon's effect!

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:16.110
What?

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.220
Shooting Star…

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:17.840
...vanished!

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:21.460
Once per your turn, I can 
remove this card from play!

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:28.250
When this effect activates, Shooting Star 
negates the attack of one of your monsters.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:30.890
Then it returns during this turn's End Phase!

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.030
Well done, Yusei!

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:36.890
Effects that negate the opponent monster's 
attack don't work against Zushin.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.560
But if it doesn't have an opponent to 
battle, Zushin's attack points become…

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.520
0 attack points!

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.510
He did it!

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:51.390
He completely stopped Zushin's attack!

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:58.980
That's true, but Shooting Star still 
can't attack Zushin the Sleeping Giant.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.320
That means…

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.890
Neither player can do anything.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:09.170
When we put Zushin in our deck, we 
anticipated that this might happen.

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:12.380
I activate the Counter Trap Fool's Dice!

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:13.330
What?

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:17.440
When your monster leaves 
the field, if I send a

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:21.180
Level 2-or-below monster in 
my hand to the graveyard...

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:25.720
...you take damage equal to the Level of the 
monster that left the field multiplied by 200 points!

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:31.010
I send Level 2 Kageningen from 
my hand to the graveyard.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.720
Shooting Star Dragon is Level 10.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:38.130
10 times 200 equals 2000 points of damage!

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:45.900
Unbelievable!

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:46.740
Yusei!

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:53.650
If Zushin the Sleeping Giant doesn't have an 
opponent to battle, its attack points become 0.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:58.460
That's why your strategy is to remove your 
monster from play so that it can't battle.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:00.150
We expected that!

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:04.090
Yusei, you only have 500 life points left.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.750
You're past Speed World 2's safety line.

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:10.720
Right now, my Speed Counter is 2.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:15.200
When it's my turn again, 
my Speed Counter will be 4.

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:23.070
At that time, if I use Speed World 2's effect 
to deal 800 points of damage, Team Taiyo wins!

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.010
I end my turn!

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.990
Return, Shooting Star Dragon!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:36.120
If the opponent gets 
another turn, Yusei loses.

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:39.560
In order to win, he has 
to beat him this turn.

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:46.030
But is there a way to take away 2500 
life points when he's up against Zushin?

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:48.090
Yusei…

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:51.240
I can finally see our victory!

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:54.040
With Zushin on our side, 
we'll definitely win!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.490
That's right.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:15:00.980
No matter how powerful your attack, Zushin's 
attack points will always be greater!

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:06.480
Traps, spells and monster effects 
don't work against Zushin!

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.700
We can do it, Zushin!

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:12.680
If we can survive for one more 
turn, we'll defeat Team 5D's!

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.170
We made it this far!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:16.760
I want to win!

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:19.750
This is the first time I wanted 
to win a duel so badly!

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:26.300
Father, I'll show you my potential!

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:31.650
The look in his eyes...

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:35.140
Yusei, you still think that you can win?

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:37.180
I'm the same as you.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:40.550
I believe in my friends and my power.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:43.120
We never give up until the very end.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.160
That's what Team 5D's is all about!

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:51.090
If we never give up, we'll 
always be victorious!

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.140
This is our final draw!

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:58.430
My…

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.350
…turn!

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:11.010
Shooting Star Dragon attacks 
Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:22.490
Even Shooting Star Dragon can't 
defeat Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:27.630
That may be true for <i>my</i> Shooting Star Dragon.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:32.470
But it's a completely different 
story for <i>our</i> Shooting Star Dragon!

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:34.940
Our?

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:40.570
I send Level 5 Earthquake Giant 
from my hand to the graveyard.

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:44.550
I use the Continuous Trap 
Monster Baton's effect!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:48.080
I see!  That's what he can do!

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:52.610
I added my monster's effect 
to Jack's trap card!

00:16:56.350 --> 00:17:01.840
Monster Baton currently has Blackwing 
- Boreas the Sharp's effect.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:06.300
By removing Boreas the Sharp from 
play, it protects my monster

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:11.010
from destruction and damage and 
destroys the monster that it battles!

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.090
What?

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:17.250
But Zushin the Sleeping Giant negates the 
effect of the monster that it battles!

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:18.830
Did you forget that, Yusei?

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:22.770
Too bad, but Zushin can't negate this effect!

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:27.260
That's because this isn't 
Shooting Star Dragon's power.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.790
It's the power that I 
received from my friends!

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:36.910
Oh yeah!  Zushin can only negate the 
effect of the monster that it battles!

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:41.040
Yusei, from the moment you 
summoned Shooting Star…

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.900
This is what you were aiming for!

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:46.290
My friends lent me this power.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:51.240
This Baton represents our 
bond that no one can break!

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:57.310
Shooting Star Dragon attacks 
Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.270
Stardust Mirage!

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.230
Zushin…

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.720
Our hope is gone.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.930
No, I'm not giving up yet!

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:39.660
As long as I survive this 
turn, Team Taiyo will win!

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:43.150
I flip over my trap card Explosive Breakout!

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:48.960
When I only have one monster and your 
Level 8-or-above monster is destroyed...

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:54.510
I can decrease my monster's attack 
points by 800 to attack a second time!

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:56.600
A second attack?

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:58.800
Shooting Star Dragon!

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.900
Stardust Mirage!

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:16.290
Taro!

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:20.000
It's over!

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:23.810
Yusei Fudo defeated the invincible Zushin!

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:27.730
It's a miraculous come-from-behind victory!

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:29.150
All right!

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.600
You did it, Yusei!

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.410
Taro!

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:42.590
Taro!

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:45.830
Did we lose?

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:46.920
Yeah…

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.600
I'm sorry.  I couldn't win.

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:51.910
Don't be stupid!

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:55.410
We were able to summon 
Zushin the Sleeping Giant!

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:57.320
That was awesome!

00:19:57.680 --> 00:19:58.490
Jin…

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:01.110
Yeah, it was great!

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:04.610
When Zushin appeared, I was so 
shocked that I almost peed my pants!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:07.070
Yoshi…

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:11.890
Well done!

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:14.060
That was great, Team Taiyo!

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:15.530
I was deeply moved!

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:18.000
Show us Zushin again!

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:22.190
Everyone is praising you.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:26.670
Your dueling has touched 
the hearts of many people.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.360
Our dueling?

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:35.920
We won the match, but it 
seems you won the duel.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.840
It was an impressive duel.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:40.910
Yeah.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:46.030
No matter how many times Team Taiyo 
sets, we rise again and shine!

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:50.220
Let's go home!

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:55.220
Let's go home and light up our own world!

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:58.080
Taro!

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:05.390
That was a wonderful duel, Team Taiyo!

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:13.270
